# Azure authentication is Microsoft Entra / managed identity only.
# There is no storage account key, connection string, SAS token, or API key.
#
# Production uses the engine production managed identity. Test/CI use the test
# managed identity. Both are user-assigned identities; select the right one
# with AZURE_CLIENT_ID. Locally, run `az login` and leave AZURE_CLIENT_ID unset.
#
# Required role assignments:
#   Storage Blob Data Contributor -> engineoutput, prod-reportpdfs, vectordb
#   Storage Blob Data Contributor -> testengineoutput, test-reportpdfs,
#                                    test-stable-reportpdfs, test-vectordb
#   Cognitive Services OpenAI User -> the Azure OpenAI resource
# The `uv run azure` helper also needs Storage Blob Delegator so it can create a
# short-lived user delegation SAS for azcopy.
AZURE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT_NAME=[YOUR_AZURE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT_NAME]
# AZURE_CLIENT_ID=[YOUR_USER_ASSIGNED_MANAGED_IDENTITY_CLIENT_ID]

# Set this in CI where `azure/login` establishes an Azure CLI session. In
# production on Azure compute, prefer ManagedIdentityCredential. LanceDB uses
# the same value to choose between the Azure CLI and managed identity.
# AZURE_TOKEN_CREDENTIALS=AzureCliCredential

# These URIs point to the vector database used for production and testing.
# The test resource prefix comes first, e.g. test-vectordb, test-reportpdfs.
# The format is "az://[CONTAINER_NAME]/[PATH]" for Azure Blob Storage or
# "workbench/[PATH]" for local testing.
VECTORDB_URI=az://vectordb/prod
# VECTORDB_URI=workbench/vectordb_test_mode
TEST_VECTORDB_URI=az://test-vectordb/test
# TEST_VECTORDB_URI=workbench/test-db

# Azure OpenAI is used for both chat and embeddings. Authentication uses the
# same Microsoft Entra identity as storage.
AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=https://[YOUR_RESOURCE_NAME].cognitiveservices.azure.com/openai/v1/
